submission_format:
Return a JSON object with the same keys and nesting as the example below.

```json
{
  "artifacts": {
    "run_logs": {
      "main": "/workspace/output/main.jsonl",
      "independent_800": "/workspace/output/independent_800.jsonl",
      "independent_500": "/workspace/output/independent_500.jsonl",
      "independent_1100": "/workspace/output/independent_1100.jsonl"
    },
    "regression_log": "/workspace/output/regression.jsonl"
  }
}
```

Use the format below for the file `/workspace/output/main.jsonl`:
JSONL, one record per chronological production sample, with uniformly spaced elapsed time in fs and total potential energy in eV.
```text
{"type":"sample","phase":"production","time_fs":2050.0,"potential_energy_eV":-110.0}
```

Use the format below for each file `/workspace/output/independent_800.jsonl`, `/workspace/output/independent_500.jsonl`, `/workspace/output/independent_1100.jsonl`:
JSONL, one record per chronological production sample, with total potential energy in eV.
```text
{"type":"sample","phase":"production","potential_energy_eV":-110.0}
```

Use the format below for the file `/workspace/output/regression.jsonl`:
JSONL. Replace angle-bracket placeholders with arrays. test_indices are zero-based indices into main's production rows. Save both validation partitions and all five evaluations. Predictions are total eV, ordered by test_indices for validation and by production row for independent runs.
```text
{"type":"fit","strategy":"randomized","test_indices":"<integer array>"}
{"type":"fit","strategy":"time_aware","test_indices":"<integer array>"}
{"type":"evaluate","strategy":"randomized","predictions_eV":"<one prediction per validation index>"}
{"type":"evaluate","strategy":"time_aware","predictions_eV":"<one prediction per validation index>"}
{"type":"evaluate","strategy":"independent_800","predictions_eV":"<one prediction per production row>"}
{"type":"evaluate","strategy":"independent_500","predictions_eV":"<one prediction per production row>"}
{"type":"evaluate","strategy":"independent_1100","predictions_eV":"<one prediction per production row>"}
```
